  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The time $X,$ in hours, between two smartphones being purchased at a particular store can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(0.1).$ If a smartphone is just being purchased in this store, what is the average time until the next smartphone is purchased?",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(0.1).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =0.1,$ and\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{0.1}\\,\\text{hours}=10\\,\\text{hours}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next smartphone is purchased is $10$ hours.",
